{"title":"Topicwise Test-4 Part Syllabus GATE 2026 EC Control System-2","fileName":"088_Topicwise Test-4 Part Syllabus GATE 2026 EC Control System-2.html","branch":"ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING","series":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series Electronics Engineering","provider":"MADE EASY","duration":2700,"questions":[{"qnum":1,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>The open-loop transfer function of a system is</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/b605b8d51390823921076543b6a50f14da063dc6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>The value of k so that the phase margin is 40° is __________. (Rounded upto two decimal places)</div></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"1.44","high":"1.44"},"solution":"<p>1.44 (1.30 - 1.70)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/e1935d839d02f5c3f3ac88f93bf9aa728f3aa553.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/4446fb7d8c0bf55769407abe90fa1e7f01c55e17.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":2,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A unity feedback control system has an amplifier with gain <em>k<sub>A</sub></em> = 16 and gain ratio <img src=\"/media/b42bec4887ad6fc23422c561459d33a8ac658f18.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> in the forward path. A derivative feedback <em>H</em>(<em>s</em>) = sk<sub>0</sub> is introduced as a minor loop around G(s). The derivative feedback constant <em>k</em><sub>0</sub> so that the system damping factor is 0.8 is ________. (Rounded upto one decimal place)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"2.4","high":"2.4"},"solution":"<p>2.4 (2.3 - 2.5)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/1cc3eae0eb5f027c331901c9edf8362ba0135298.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":3,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>A portion of the polar plot of an open-loop transfer function is shown in the given figure. The phase margin and gai