plitude of steady state response will have maximum value and the maximum value of steady state output are respectively</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 7.625 rad/sec and 1.201</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 5.658 rad/sec and 1.155</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 5.658 rad/sec and 1.8</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 7.625 rad/sec and 1.8</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/c4a1ac976a8a97d48c9d65fa4656c62c729293f4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/9bd03bd38bde17c0e649c10ab202548bb2a4b9fb.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":12,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>The Nyquist plot of an all pole second order open loop system is shown in figure. The transfer function of the system is</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/3963df956f73a07ec5ab09666a41f2f4e0d6e7f5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/07691c59d09a9ff170ac28d4223b75695e6f3375.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/d998df07b07527b34cfcc6d44ecb7494d531499c.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/f8e82fcd83042ce781c69af2f13875fa40d1e9ff.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/a832e34d8874bb9c15ee48657a94b0f0f82ca5b2.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/20f7aae4b3e09aa20175d489aba139a255071ff5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/70ad752fe42059f43eee2eafd523c548eee5184c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":13,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>The open loop transfer function of a unity feedback control system is given by the expression</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/dee0e3e239ed99f04087c2a408e7d39cbbad394c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>If <em>N</em> is the number of encirclements of (–1 + <em>j</em>0) point by the Nyquist plot in the anti-clockwise direction, then which of the following statements is correct?</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> System is stable with <em>N</em> = 2</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> System is stable with <em>N</em> = 0.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> System is unstable with <em>N</em> = –2</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> System is unstable with <em>N</em> = 0</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/81033633167b0ca318ccdd1b2950703455ca33c0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/77a87b1cb94316a5523d295b929b5fe320a5d4f6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<p> </p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":14,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>The state space representation of an LTI system is described as,</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/a1b0845222c7d57687b55e83dee416626a920917.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>\n<div>The value of k to yield a 15% overshoot with a settling time of 0.6 sec for a step input is _______.<br />\n(Rounded upto two decimal places)</div></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"41.57","high":"41.57"},"solution":"<p>41.57 (41.55 - 41.59)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/6b6aa1a64addd25eff67a678896870d174ad6875.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/0a3a21c67916642d783930ddb34e528bb2cb6b84.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":15,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>The system described by the state mode